1. Scope and definitions

"Edge0 Materials" means the Edge0-specific model contributions expressly
identified in an accompanying release scope record as licensed under this
License, and only to the extent that Edge0 owns or is authorized to license
rights in those contributions. These may include original model modifications,
adapters, training deltas, and model-specific documentation. Merely naming a
repository does not establish ownership of every file or of an entire model.

"Upstream Materials" means Qwen materials and any other third-party materials
included in or required by a release. Their existing licenses remain in
effect. They are not relicensed as Edge0 property by this License.

"Covered Model" means a model incorporating Edge0 Materials, including a
modified, fine-tuned, quantized, pruned, converted, or merged version, but only
insofar as exercising rights in Edge0 Materials requires Edge0's permission.
This definition does not extend to an independently obtained upstream model
or an independent work that does not incorporate protected Edge0 Materials.

"Outputs" means text, code, images, data, or other results generated by running
a Covered Model. It does not mean copies of weights, adapters, or other Edge0
Materials merely extracted or reproduced through a model.

"Commercial Model Offering" has the limited meaning set out in Section 4.
"You" means the person or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

This License does not apply to framework or inference-engine code already
licensed under Apache-2.0, MIT, or another separately identified license, or
to earlier releases not expressly designated under this License.

2. Upstream rights are preserved

You must comply with every applicable upstream license when using or
redistributing Upstream Materials or works derived from them. The applicable
Qwen license is reproduced unchanged in third-party/Qwen-LICENSE.txt. The
release scope record must identify the upstream source and applicable
license, distinguishing a license-reference revision from any independently
verified training or conversion revision.

This License neither replaces that license nor waives any Qwen restriction,
attribution requirement, or requirement for a separate Qwen authorization.
Permission from Edge0 is not permission from Qwen, and permission from Qwen
is not permission from Edge0 for separately protected Edge0 Materials.

If an upstream license and this License cannot both be satisfied, no right
to the conflicting use of Edge0 Materials is granted here. Nothing in this
License reduces rights You hold independently in Upstream Materials. An
upstream license does not acquire additional Edge0 conditions merely because
its text or materials are distributed beside this License.

All permissions and examples below are subject to applicable upstream terms.
An activity that is free of an Edge0 fee may still require Qwen authorization.

3. Broad community permission

Subject to Sections 2, 4, and 5, Edge0 grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive,
no-charge, royalty-free copyright license to use, run, study, reproduce,
modify, fine-tune, quantize, prune, convert, merge, evaluate, publish, and
redistribute Edge0 Materials and modifications of them. This grant continues
for the duration of the applicable copyright, subject to Section 9.

No separate Edge0 permission, registration, user-count threshold, or revenue
threshold applies to an activity unless it is a Commercial Model Offering.
In particular, this License permits:

(a) personal use, including local deployment and private experimentation;
(b) research, education, teaching, benchmarking, and publication of findings;
(c) community development and noncommercial sharing of original or modified
    models, adapters, quantizations, and related tools;
(d) internal organizational use, including use by businesses, when You are
    not making a Commercial Model Offering;
(e) use by employees, freelancers, creators, and other individuals to produce
    work for which they are paid, without providing customers access to the
    model or distributing the model as a Commercial Model Offering; and
(f) commercial use of Outputs, and use of a model as an incidental component
    of a product or a domain-specific tool, where the activity does not fall
    within Section 4.

Edge0 does not require disclosure of Your source code, private data, training
data, prompts, or modifications. You may keep modifications private. Edge0
does not require an interface badge, mandatory telemetry, or prior approval
for research or benchmarking. Upstream obligations remain unaffected.

Voluntary donations unconnected to access, features, service levels, or model
delivery, and reimbursement limited to documented copying or delivery costs,
do not by themselves make noncommercial community sharing a Commercial Model
Offering. A subscription or service fee cannot be renamed a donation to
qualify for this exception.

4. Limited commercial reservation

You must obtain a separate written commercial license from Edge0 before
making any of the following Commercial Model Offerings:

(a) Model sales and paid distribution: selling, renting, or licensing access
    to, or copies of, a Covered Model, its weights, or an adapter or delta
    incorporating Edge0 Materials; or distributing them in a paid bundle
    whose principal value proposition is access to that model. Unrestricted
    community donations and cost reimbursement described in Section 3 are
    excluded.

(b) Commercial model services: operating a service for third parties that
    offers language-model inference or fine-tuning as a capability in its own
    right, through an API, hosted endpoint, hosted general-purpose model
    interface, or equivalent arrangement, and that is financed by access or
    usage fees, a subscription, advertising, or sponsorship tied to that
    service. Customers must be able meaningfully to control inference inputs
    or fine-tuning inputs. A single-purpose domain tool or an incidental
    assistant feature is not covered by this paragraph merely because it
    uses a model to generate task-specific results.

(c) Commercial independent coding or office assistants: offering an
    independent product primarily designed for AI-assisted coding or office
    productivity that uses a Covered Model and is financed by sales, access
    or usage fees, subscriptions, advertising, or sponsorship tied to the
    product. This applies whether inference is hosted or runs on a user's
    device. A single-purpose tool, an assistant primarily serving another
    domain, or an incidental feature of a product with another primary
    purpose is excluded from this paragraph.

Merely earning income, working for a company, receiving research funding,
selling Outputs, or performing a task for a client does not by itself fall
within this Section. Neither does selling unrelated software or hardware
merely because it can run a model, without a paid model bundle or another
offering described above. Private model installation, training, or integration
services are permitted unless the actual arrangement includes a model sale,
paid distribution, or an offering described above. A paid custom adapter or
delta incorporating Edge0 Materials is covered by paragraph (a).

These reservations apply only to rights Edge0 controls. They do not authorize
Edge0 to license Qwen rights or to charge for rights independently available
from another rights holder. A separate Edge0 commercial license must identify
the rights it grants and does not waive upstream obligations unless the
relevant upstream rights holder has expressly authorized that waiver.

5. Redistribution and attribution

When redistributing Edge0 Materials or modifications containing them, You must:

(a) include this License and all applicable upstream license texts and notices;
(b) preserve applicable copyright and attribution notices;
(c) identify Your material modifications and the responsible modifier in a
    reasonably accessible change record or model documentation; and
(d) tell recipients which materials are subject to this License and which
    remain governed by separate upstream licenses. You must not represent
    this License as a replacement for the Qwen license.

You may choose the license for Your own additions, provided You identify them
separately and do not purport to remove the conditions governing Edge0 or
Upstream Materials. Recipients may obtain the same rights in Edge0 Materials
directly under this License. You cannot grant a recipient rights You do not
have, or impose a term that denies a recipient rights granted directly here.

You are not required by Edge0 to publish private changes or to put branding
in a user interface. Reasonable origin statements in distributed model
documentation are sufficient for Edge0 attribution; Qwen's separate interface
attribution conditions, if applicable, must still be followed.

6. Outputs and independent works

Edge0 claims no ownership of Outputs solely because they were generated with
a Covered Model, and imposes no Edge0 fee, attribution duty, or use restriction
on those Outputs. You may use, share, sell, and use Outputs to train other
models, subject to applicable law, upstream terms, and third-party rights.
This is not a representation that every Output is protectable or free of
third-party claims. If an Output contains protected pre-existing material,
its independent legal requirements remain applicable.

This License creates no rights over Your independently developed work or
over material merely processed by a Covered Model. Independently obtaining
and modifying a Qwen model without using protected Edge0 Materials does not
by itself bring that work under this License.

