9. Termination and continuity

If You materially breach this License, the rights granted by Edge0 under it
terminate. They are automatically reinstated when a first breach is fully
cured within 30 days after You discover it or receive notice of it, whichever
is earlier. Reinstatement for a later breach requires Edge0's written consent.
Reinstatement does not excuse a past claim or waive an upstream condition.

Termination applies only to Edge0's grant. Upstream rights and obligations
are determined by the relevant upstream licenses. Recipients who remain in
compliance do not lose their direct rights because of Your breach.

Edge0 may publish new license versions for future releases, but doing so does
not change the terms already granted for an existing release. Existing valid
grants under Apache-2.0, MIT, or another license are not withdrawn by publishing
this License. You may rely on rights You already validly hold.

